## item 9 (enum-niche tail) — bare-`def`-as-Fn-value HOF regression lock.
##
## The 5a-era item-9 filing claimed "a bare top-level `def` passed as a Fn
## value emits `@__Future_*` → llc undefined value." A read-only scoping pass
## (2026-06-14) found that MISDIAGNOSIS: `call_with(inc, 5)` (bare def passed
## as an `Fn(Int): Int` value) already builds, llc-passes, and runs == 6 at
## HEAD. The real undefined-symbol was `@__qz_gen_yield_capture` (the Yield
## default handler in std/gen.qz) dangling on a STALE backup binary — fixed
## separately by gating the Yield install on `uses_yield`.
##
## This is the forward regression lock for the DIRECT bare-def-as-Fn-value
## form the 5a `option_some(inc).unwrap()` dodge avoided: pass a bare top-
## level def straight into an `Fn(Int): Int` parameter, bind it to a const,
## nest it (call_twice), and pass a lambda alongside. All must compile,
## llc-pass (no undefined value), link, run, exit 0, print "ALL OK".
##
## Returns 0 on success; a distinct non-zero code per failed assertion.

def inc(x: Int): Int = x + 1

def call_with(f: Fn(Int): Int, n: Int): Int = f(n)

def call_twice(f: Fn(Int): Int, n: Int): Int = f(f(n))

def main(): Int
  # Bare top-level def passed directly into an Fn(Int): Int parameter.
  if call_with(inc, 5) != 6
    return 1
  end

  # Bare def bound to a const (const-by-default), then passed.
  f = inc
  if call_with(f, 5) != 6
    return 2
  end

  # Nested application of the bare-def value.
  if call_twice(inc, 5) != 7
    return 3
  end

  # Lambda passed alongside, same parameter slot.
  if call_with(x -> x + 1, 5) != 6
    return 4
  end

  puts("ALL OK")
  return 0
end
